    <title>Strip The City S2 - "Venice"</title>
    <desc>Engineers strip away the waters of Venice to reveal how ancient wooden piles and modern sea barriers protect the historic city from sinking.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005065441 +0000" stop="20261005074847 +0000">
    <title>Strip The City S2 - "New York"</title>
    <desc>The layers of America's largest metropolis are peeled back to show how skyscrapers withstand high winds and subways navigate a subterranean labyrinth.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005074847 +0000" stop="20261005080202 +0000">
    <title>Past, Present, Future S1 - "...of Surgery"</title>
    <desc>Hundreds of years before antibiotics, the legendary Chinese physician Hua Tuo performed miraculous surgical operations. Today, doctors perform increasingly complex surgery that is only possible with the support of advanced robotics.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005080202 +0000" stop="20261005090430 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Across Oceans"</title>
    <desc>Throughout history, human society has run on trade. The innovations that allowed faster and more accurate oceanic travel revolutionized the world. New inventions now help people and goods move on the water faster for recreation and commerce.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005090430 +0000" stop="20261005101013 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Across Continents"</title>
    <desc>Never in the history of humanity have so many of us been mobile. New innovations propel us into the world of self-driving cars and high-speed trains.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005101013 +0000" stop="20261005111941 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Into the Skies"</title>
    <desc>Growth in air transportation is set to soar, carrying over 10 billion passengers every year by 2050. To cope requires us to radically rethink aircraft design. Join us as we look into the world's most innovative research and development labs.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005111941 +0000" stop="20261005122740 +0000">
    <title>Speed S1 - "Into Space"</title>
    <desc>The most innovative area of human motion lies not on Earth, but with the exploration of space. Meet the private space entrepreneurs jostling to offer the tantalizing prospect of cheap, frequent travel beyond the atmosphere into Earth orbit.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005122740 +0000" stop="20261005133203 +0000">
    <title>Digits S1 - "Connecting to the Future"</title>
    <desc>Muller escorts viewers to the physical heart of the Internet, revealing the very first message sent by UCLA professor Leonard Kleinrock, and demonstrating how Internet co-creators Vint Cerf and Bob Kahn devised a common protocol language.</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005133203 +0000" stop="20261005143759 +0000">
    <title>Digits S1 - "Man vs. Machine"</title>
    <desc>Get a sneak peek into how the Internet of Things will soon dominate daily life. As Edward Snowden provocatively points out, “TV is a medium that you watch. The Internet is a medium that watches you as you watch it.”</desc>
  </programme>
  
<programme channel="6a1610bebdf296985fd95603-6668b2b5e4f56766e556a413" start="20261005143759 +0000" stop="20261005154156 +0000">
    <title>Digits S1 - "Guardians of the Web"</title>
    <desc>Explore how our reliance on the web creates vulnerability to everything from cyber theft to an Internet system failure. Muller introduces viewers to “white hat” hackers, the U.S. Secret Service’s cybercrime division and even West Point soldiers.</desc>
  </programme>
  
